<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n487" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγη</span></b> , 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγᾱ</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰγ]</span>, ἡ<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, ʽἄγαμαἰ</span>”
				<i>wonder, amazement,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hom.
				</span></i>
			 only in phrase 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγη μ᾽ ἔχει</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					21.221
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.227
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				16.243
			</span></i>: glossed by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τιμή, σεβασμός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>envy, malice,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Φθόνῳ καὶ ἄγῃ χρεώμενος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					6.61
				</span></i>
			; of the gods, <i>jealousy,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μή τις ἄγα θεόθεν κνεφάσῃ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Ag.</u>
					131
				</span></i>
			: pl. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄγαις,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζηλώσεσιν</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				85
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
